-- A thread may have an owner, and so may each comment in it. The condition tests that the thread's
-- own `owner` is present, and then, inside the filter over the thread's comments, reads `name`
-- through each comment's `owner` with a plain dot.
--
-- The compiler accepts it. Inside the filter a bare `owner` is the comment's, which no test has
-- shown present. Without `owner is some and` the same filter draws V11: "'owner.name' reads through
-- 'owner', which may be absent".
act Member { name: text }

act Thread { owner: one Member? }

act Comment {
    owner: one Member?
    thread: one Thread
}

shape ThreadOfAda = Thread where owner is some and exists (comments where owner.name == "Ada")
